sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as codex@node-2 (CLI)
    participant MA as mailbox MCP (node-2)
    participant DA as worker daemon (node-2)
    participant H as hub relay + mail store
    participant DB as worker daemon (node-1)
    participant MB as mailbox MCP (node-1)
    participant B as claude@node-1 (CLI in tmux)

    A->>MA: mail_send(to, subject, body, task)
    MA->>DA: call with operation id (agent socket)
    DA->>DA: stamp sender and current turn
    DA->>H: forward on the SSH stream
    H->>H: check identity, peers, kind, hop, thread, size
    alt refused
        H-->>DA: refusal with reason (event recorded)
        DA-->>MA: refusal
        MA-->>A: tool error with reason
    else accepted
        H->>H: store message, from_kind = agent, hop from turn inputs
        H-->>DA: message id (repeat of the op id returns the same id)
        DA-->>MA: message id
        MA-->>A: tool result with id
        alt node-1 stream up
            H->>DB: deliver frame
        else node-1 stream down
            H->>H: keep message queued (until expires)
            Note over H,DB: stream opens again (reconnect, daemon or relay restart)
            DB->>H: sync: spool ids, tombstones, pending acks
            H->>H: record pending acks, reconcile queued and delivered, expire old mail
            H->>DB: deliver frame only for ids neither in spool nor tombstoned, oldest first
        end
        DB->>DB: append to spool of claude (drop if tombstoned)
        DB->>H: turn_begin for claude
        alt admission refused (switch, budget, no slot)
            H-->>DB: refused, mail stays unread
        else admitted
            H-->>DB: turn id
            alt agent in a turn
                B->>DB: Stop hook asks for a continuation
                DB-->>B: block the stop once: call mail_inbox
            else agent idle, no question, operator not attached
                DB->>B: tmux send-keys -l fixed wake line, Enter
                DB->>DB: wait 8 s for turn start or mail_inbox, retry at most 2
            else question open or state unknown
                DB->>DB: no wake, sweep every 30 s
            end
            B->>MB: mail_inbox()
            MB->>DB: read spool
            DB-->>MB: unread envelopes, marked retrieved in this turn
            MB-->>B: envelopes (from another agent)
            alt turn ends normally
                B->>DB: turn end signal
                DB->>H: turn end with retrieved ids (acked)
                DB->>DB: delete envelopes, keep tombstone ids
            else turn lost or CLI exited
                DB->>DB: keep envelopes, offer again as redelivered
            end
        end
    end
